# AniCast UI

Before changing UI, read `docs/FRONTEND_DESIGN_RULES.md` and
`docs/BRAND_UI_TECH_SPEC.md`. They override generic framework and design advice.

- Preserve App Router, Server Components by default, CSS Modules, Phosphor Icons,
  semantic CSS variables, and the existing i18n system.
- Do not introduce Tailwind, shadcn/ui, a new palette, icon family, or UI dependency
  unless the user explicitly requests that architectural change.
- Inspect the closest existing route and shared component before adding a pattern.
- Design applicable loading, empty, unavailable, pending, success, error, disabled,
  focus, mobile, and retry states.
- Never display success before backend confirmation or discard useful input after an
  error.
- Prefer native HTML semantics; preserve keyboard access, visible focus, logical DOM
  order, meaningful labels, and AA contrast.
- Keep cleanup scoped to the requested change and report unrelated design debt.

For review, classify user-facing failures by impact and state which browser,
keyboard, viewport, accessibility, and build checks were actually performed.
